# Poka-yoke and adversarial review

False CLEAR (unsafe aisle marked clear / AUTO_CLEAR) is the red-line failure. Make the wrong action impossible; do not add a warning and continue.

## Poka-yoke (must remain true)

- No AUTO_CLEAR if caption inconsistent, NEAR_MISS, named hazards, CONFIDENCE=LOW, UNCLEAR nonempty, view blocked, or YOLO person+vehicle without HIGH PATH_CLEAR.
- Operator cannot “gate_ok” on HOLD (API 400 + UI disabled).
- Override requires a non-`agree` reason. AUTO_ALERT → CLEAR needs `confirm_escape`.
- Ingest: filename regex + known scene_id only; custom_prompt ≤800; no YouTube/http file paths.
- `scripts/push_both.sh` refuses clips/secrets and fails if origin or github push fails.

## Adversarial review (every change)

Before you commit: run attacks that should fail closed (false CLEAR, illegal operator POST, bad filename, 801-char prompt, YouTube path, invented VSS routes, Canary wiring, hardcoded GPU host). Clone https://github.com/vast-data/vast-builders-challenge and run `./scripts/run_adversarial.sh`. Record results in `.cursor/adversarial/` with Attack / Expected / Result / Fix. If an attack succeeds, fix it before any other work. Happy-path tests alone are not enough.
